questions.stem:
A stage manager cues lights with this method:
public static void count(int n) { if (n == 0) return; System.out.print(n); count(n - 1); }
Calling count(3) runs the cue. What is printed?

A party planner stacks favor boxes with this method:
public static int fact(int n) { if (n == 0) return 1; return n * fact(n - 1); }
What does fact(4) return?

A cashier adds coin piles with this method:
public static int sum(int n) { if (n == 0) return 0; return n + sum(n - 1); }
What does sum(3) return?

A lab models cell doubling with this method:
public static int pow(int b, int e) { if (e == 0) return 1; return b * pow(b, e - 1); }
What does pow(2, 3) return?

A combinatorics helper needs its missing step:
public static int fact(int n) { if (n == 0) return 1; _____; }
Which line completes the method?

A scheduler computes fact(3) as 0 with this method:
public static int fact(int n) { if (n == 0) return 0; return n * fact(n - 1); }
Which statement identifies the fault?

A rocket club finishes its launch cue:
public static void count(int n) { if (n <= 0) return; System.out.print(n); _____; }
Which line belongs in the blank?

A botanist counts petals with this method:
public static int fib(int n) { if (n <= 1) return n; return fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2); }
What integer does fib(6) return?

A print shop measures banners with this method:
public static int letters(String s) { if (s.length() == 0) return 0; return 1 + letters(s.substring(1)); }
What does letters("hello") return?

A launch controller overflows the stack with this cue:
public static void launch(int n) { if (n <= 0) return; System.out.print(n); launch(n); }
Calling launch(3) crashes. Which statement identifies the fault?

A cashier writes a sum that must work for every non-negative input, including sum(0):
public static int sum(int n) { _____; return n + sum(n - 1); }
Which base case belongs in the blank?

A shelter counts bunny ears with this method:
public static int ears(int bunnies) { if (bunnies == 0) return 0; return 2 + ears(bunnies - 1); }
What does ears(4) return?

A choir layers echoes with this method:
public static void chant(int n) { if (n == 0) return; System.out.print(n); chant(n - 1); System.out.print(n); }
Calling chant(3) performs the piece. What is printed?

A ledger crashes printing sum(0) with this method:
public static int sum(int n) { if (n == 1) return 1; return n + sum(n - 1); }
Which statement identifies the fault?

A garden model needs its missing combination step:
public static int fib(int n) { if (n <= 1) return n; _____; }
Which line completes the method?

A researcher counts every fib call, including the first, for this method:
public static int fib(int n) { if (n <= 1) return n; return fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2); }
How many total calls run while computing fib(5)?

A sign painter reverses words with this method:
public static void spell(String s) { if (s.length() == 0) return; spell(s.substring(1)); System.out.print(s.charAt(0)); }
Calling spell("cat") paints the wall. What is printed?

A phone book searches its upper half with this method:
public static int find(int[] a, int t, int lo, int hi) {
  if (lo > hi) return -1;
  int mid = (lo + hi) / 2;
  if (a[mid] == t) return mid;
  if (a[mid] < t) { _____; }
  return find(a, t, lo, mid - 1);
}
Which line belongs in the blank?

A directory search misses present names with this method:
public static int find(int[] a, int t, int lo, int hi) {
  if (lo > hi) return -1;
  int mid = (lo + hi) / 2;
  if (a[mid] == t) return mid;
  if (a[mid] < t) { find(a, t, mid + 1, hi); }
  return find(a, t, lo, mid - 1);
}
Which statement identifies the fault?
